### In-File Spell Checking

This is the primary way you'll interact with the extension.

¬TODO 111 Add all images for correcting a file here

{{::il.Vscode_CodeSpellChecker_File_1_img}}





### What you see

Misspelled words are underlined with a **blue squiggle** (customizable in your VS Code theme). The check happens automatically as you type — no manual action needed.

### How to respond to a flagged word

| Action | Method | Result |
|--------|--------|--------|
| **See suggestions** | Hover over the underlined word | A popup appears with suggested corrections |
| **Apply a fix** | Click a suggestion in the hover popup, or press `Ctrl+.` and select one | The word is replaced |
| **Add to workspace dictionary** | Press `Ctrl+.` → **"Add '{word}' to workspace dictionary"** | Never flagged again in this repository |
| **Add to user dictionary** | Press `Ctrl+.` → **"Add '{word}' to user dictionary"** | Never flagged again across all your VS Code projects |
| **Ignore once** | Press `Ctrl+.` → **"Ignore '{word}'"** | Hides the underline for this session only |

> **Tip:** Favour the **workspace dictionary** for project-specific terms like `tsstp`, `tsvar`, or `Vscode`. Use the **user dictionary** for your name, company name, or other terms that appear in every project. Was toggleable 

